Well, you get the elvish advantages, of course - high INT and WIS
possibilities, sleep resistance at XL 4, and one extra - you can put
critters to sleep if you attack bare-handed.

I personally like droven necromancers - sickness and drain resistance
are nice (not super-critical, but nice), and they have the priest's
built-in curse-detection ability.

Like them, mind you. Success, no. Enjoy, yes.

